{{- /*
reviews.gohtml is the panel's FIRST screen of ADR 0030's shape, and it is almost
empty on purpose.

Every other page in this package is rendered on the server from the Query layer.
This one renders a shell and lets a script fill it from /admin/v1 — the same
admin API an external client uses — because that is what ADR 0030 decided the
panel becomes. The migration starts here rather than with an existing screen: a
section nobody has yet is the one where a new shape costs no rewrite, and the
review module's admin API was already complete (ADR 0071 to 0074).

The noscript block is not a courtesy. A page whose whole content arrives by
script shows an operator an empty box when the script fails to load, and an
empty moderation queue is the one answer this feature must never give wrongly.
*/ -}}
{{ define "body" }}
<h1>{{ .Title }}</h1>

<noscript>
  <p class="notice">This screen is a client of the admin API and needs JavaScript.
  The same data is at <code>/admin/v1/reviews</code>.</p>
</noscript>

<div id="reviews-app" data-api="{{ .APIPrefix }}">
  <p id="reviews-status">Loading…</p>
</div>

<script src="{{ .ReviewsScript }}" defer></script>
{{ end }}
